# WHITELIST, not a blocklist.
#
# This directory is a working root that also contains 20-odd checked-out
# repositories and a large amount of one-off material generated while solving
# problems -- handoff notes, probe scripts, patched copies of other people's
# launch files, logs. Almost none of it is something this repository should
# carry, and a blocklist would let the next one through by default.
#
# So: everything is ignored, and the bootstrap is added back by name. If you
# add a file that belongs here, add it below too.

*

# --- the bootstrap itself --------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!README.md
!tari.bash
!dgpy_install.sh
!colcon_defaults.yaml
!sim.repos
!acq.repos
!hw.repos
!site.repos

# --- container tooling: NOT tracked here -----------------------------------
# ros2_docker.sh, entrypoint.sh and docker/ are one unit, and it is not part of
# the bootstrap. It exists because one development machine runs Arch, where ROS
# Iron is not packaged; the native Ubuntu path this repository describes needs
# none of it.
#
# docker/ could not be tracked in any case -- its two subdirectories are git
# repositories on gitlab.afresearchlab.com, so committing them would create
# gitlinks no clone could resolve -- and splitting the unit, with the scripts
# here and the images they build over there, would be worse than either whole.
# They belong together, wherever they end up.

# --- never ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by tari.bash --phase env, machine-specific by construction.
tari_setup.bash
